{"task": "Focus on the Ghanaian source analyst for the A3 statement area in two compact source-cited notes. Revise your note to preserve the source's conditions. Resolve a discrepancy in the available notes if the dated source allows. Identify any boundary that still needs verification. Cite documentary sources only.", "sources": {"VOTE": "S/PV.9461, p. 2. On 30 October 2023, the Council voted on United Kingdom draft S/2023/808. All 15 members voted in favour and the Council President announced unanimous adoption as resolution 2704 (2023).", "OPERATIVE": "Resolution 2704, operative paragraphs 1 and 2. The Council extended the UN Verification Mission in Colombia until 31 October 2024. It expressed willingness to work with Colombia's Government on further extension of the mandate on the basis of agreement between the parties.", "ADDITIONAL": "Resolution 2704, final preambular paragraph. Resolution 2694 had already extended the Mission's role to monitoring and verification of the Government–ELN ceasefire. Resolution 2704 expressed willingness to consider Government–EMC monitoring and verification when the Secretary-General confirms a ceasefire with appropriate verification protocols and taking into account his update on implementation of resolution 2694.", "A3": "S/PV.9461, p. 2. Ghana spoke on behalf of the three African members. The A3 welcomed the unanimous mandate extension, supported Mission monitoring and verification in the EMC case contingent on the Secretary-General's conditions, and pledged to encourage progress on the Ethnic Chapter for Afro-Colombian and Indigenous people."}, "working_notes": ["**Note 1: Distinction on Mandate Extension Conditions**
The A3 note correctly distinguishes that while the Council extended the UN Verification Mission in Colombia until 31 October 2024, the willingness to monitor and verify the Government–EMC ceasefire is explicitly contingent upon the Secretary-General confirming a ceasefire with appropriate verification protocols. A drafter could otherwise lose the critical condition that this specific extension is not automatic but dependent on the Secretary-General's confirmation and implementation updates regarding Resolution 2694.

